From fb1fe113042c7ea069f4fd2670be823d619b2077 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-v6 <v6@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 18:37:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] v6: widen F64 register class to xmm8-15, XMM-honoring
 sqrt/fabs/FP loads/stores

- F64 register pool now spans xmm2-xmm15 (14 regs, was 6): the allocator
  previously spilled nbody's 58 FP intervals despite xmm8-15 being free and
  codegen-safe (scratch only touches xmm0/1/2). phys_reg_name/is_xmm_reg
  extended; the assembler already encodes the REX-extension bank.
- SqrtF64/F32 and FabsF64/F32 now honor XMM-allocated destinations (the sqrt
  in nbody's hot loop was a movq %xmm,%rax; movq %rax,%xmm0 round-trip).
  fabs is now a single andpd/andps against a rodata mask (was movabsq+movq+
  andpd).
- F64/F32 loads and stores with materialized/computed pointers now emit
  movsd/movss directly into/from the XMM home (was movq (%ptr),%rax;
  movq %rax,%xmmN and the store mirror).

Measured: mandelbrot 2.87x -> 2.13x vs gcc. nbody FP arithmetic now stays in
XMM (round-trips 26 -> 13), still bounded by un-strength-reduced i*56 address
computation (next step).

Validation: regression 127/127, correctness 50/50, intrinsics 3/3; nbody/
spectral_norm/mandelbrot/struct_copy bit-exact vs gcc.
